              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='20337' id='2897' type-v2='text' w='77392' x='22062' y='14494'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>Context</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontsize='4'>Æ </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'>Sample Size:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'>- </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontname='Arial'>Some occasions have sample size below the threshold</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'> to consider the information as reliable (data in blue)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'>- It’s</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontname='Arial'> possible to remove</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'> these cases by changing the &apos;Sample Size&apos; filter to ‘Above Threshold’ only</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontsize='4'>Æ </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'>%Customers</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'>- This KPI is calculated using the </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontname='Arial'>unique number of customers</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'> as the denominator, which may lead to the total being above 100%</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontsize='4'>Æ </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'>Confidence Interval</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'>- Although not shown in the table, GMV and Orders have the</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontname='Arial'> same confidence intervals </run>
                  <run fontname='Arial'>as presented in the ‘Country Overview - Performance’ charts</run>
                </formatted-text>
